\f1\fs22 by a pretty young blonde with pig-tails, a deeply tanned complexion and a wide bright smile. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable> I\'92m not working the wards now. They decided working on the dead was the best option for me. Just as long as everything gets done, they let me do what I like.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Cracker first bumped into his contact in the world of pathology when he was contracted for regular maintenance in the public medical centres of The Pale. The first year intern had knocked off for the day, stumbled out of the staff exit and staggered off into the night. Hours later they crossed paths again in the quarter when he spied her, arms littered with sticky and variously coloured patches, dancing solo in the street. She had been hyper-patched by a crew of scoundrels and by that time Cracker found her, she was completely incoherent and unable, even, to remove the patches. Her pre-rape stagger saw Kathy a prime candidate for abuse and although his natural reaction should have been leave her to her fate, Cracker adopted the role of protector and managed to fight off a few would-be assailants to get her back to the hospital dorm intact. For the next couple of years, he would fetch patches for her, limiting the good doctor\'92s exposure to the vultures on the street, but had lost contact when she was transferred to the Health, Respite and Retreat Zone.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Patches were perfect recreation for the self-medicating urban professional. Hallucinogens, stimulants, depressants, performance enhancers and anything else medical miscreants can cook up were infused into patches, adhered to the upper arm and a party ensues. Some patches were medication masala, a combination of many flavours, but Kathy\'92s favourite was \'93Organised Party\'94. You could plan the perfect night out with the release of different drugs at specific times, seamlessly slipping from one buzz to the other or into periods of absolute clarity then plunging into psychedelic hilarity. Unless you had been the victim of hyper-patching, the effects begin to wear off directly upon removal, but Kathy patched all day, everyday, her work schedule neatly wedged in between periods of incoherence of one type or another. She rolled up her sleeve, closed her eyes and fished her hand around in the box, picking a patch at random.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable> She slipped into incoherence and curled up on the floor. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Precisely half an hour had passed and Dr Logan burst back in to life, her mind perfectly clear. \'93Well, I\'92ve got 40 minutes of lucidity so let\'92s look at the results.\'94\
